<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/05KY">Example <span data-tag="05KY">8.7.1.9</span> <span class="named">(Fiberwise idempotent-completion)</span>.</a> Suppose we are given a commutative diagram of simplicial sets </p>
<div class="equation" id="05KZ">
<span class="equation-label"><a data-tag="05KZ" href="/tag/05KZ">8.95</a></span>
<div>\begin{equation}  \begin{gathered}\label{equation:fiberwise-idempotent-completion} \xymatrix@R =50pt@C=50pt{ \operatorname{\mathcal{E}}\ar [dr]_{ U } \ar [rr]^-{H} &amp;  &amp;  \widehat{\operatorname{\mathcal{E}}} \ar [dl]^{ \widehat{U} } \\ &amp;  \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}, &amp;  } \end{gathered} \end{equation}</div>
</div>
<p> where $U$ and $\widehat{U}$ are inner fibrations. We say that (<a data-tag="05KZ" href="/tag/05KZ">8.95</a>) <em>exhibits $\widehat{\operatorname{\mathcal{E}}}$ as a fiberwise idempotent-completion of $\operatorname{\mathcal{E}}$</em> if it exhibits $\widehat{\operatorname{\mathcal{E}}}$ as a $\{  \operatorname{N}_{\bullet }( \operatorname{Idem}) \} $-cocompletion of $\operatorname{\mathcal{E}}$, in the sense of Definition <a data-tag="05KR" href="/tag/05KR">8.7.1.5</a>; here $\operatorname{Idem}$ is the category introduced in Construction <a data-tag="03ZN" href="/tag/03ZN">8.5.2.7</a>. </p>
</article>
